> **Heads-up:** Note that the category `male` is the baseline level under this framework for $X_{i, \texttt{sex}}$.

**Q1.3.5.** Now that we already defined the response of interest, our regressors, and a more adequate model. What is the training sample's modelling equation? What is its main characteristic on the left-hand side?

<!--
# BEGIN QUESTION
name: Q1-3-5-reasoning
manual: true
-->

**ANSWER:**

<!-- # BEGIN SOLUTION -->

> *For $i = 1, \dots, n$, the training sample's modelling equation for this the Binary Logistic regression model is:*
> $$\log\left(\frac{p_i}{1 - p_i}\right) = \beta_0 + \beta_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} + \beta_2 X_{i, \texttt{sex}}.$$

> *The main characteristic of this modelling equation on the left-side is the GLM's link function: the log of odds of survival $p_i$ versus non-survival $1 - p_i$.*

<!-- # END SOLUTION -->

