## Q1.6. Coefficient Interpretation

Via your model fitted and stored in `titanic_model`, interpret the estimated coefficients associated to those significant explanatory variables (i.e., the second main inquiry). **Use an adequate scale.**

<!--
# BEGIN QUESTION
name: Q1-6-reasoning
manual: true
-->

**ANSWER:**

<!-- # BEGIN SOLUTION -->

> *We have that:*
$$
X_{i, \texttt{sex}} =
\begin{cases}
1 \; \; \; \; \text{if the passenger is female},\\
0 \; \; \; \; \mbox{otherwise},
\end{cases}
$$
> *and*
\begin{gather*}
\log\left(\frac{\hat{p}_i}{1 - \hat{p}_i}\right) = \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} + \hat{\beta}_2 X_{i, \texttt{sex}} \\
\frac{\hat{p}_i}{1 - \hat{p}_i} = \exp \left( \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} + \hat{\beta}_2 X_{i, \texttt{sex}} \right) \\
\frac{\hat{p}_i}{1 - \hat{p}_i} = \exp \left( \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} \right) \exp \left( \hat{\beta}_2 X_{i, \texttt{sex}} \right) \\
\frac{\hat{p}_i}{1 - \hat{p}_i} = \exp \left( \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} \right) \exp \big( \underbrace{2.461}_{\hat{\beta}_2} X_{i, \texttt{sex}} \big) \\
\frac{\hat{p}_i}{1 - \hat{p}_i} = \exp \left( \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} \right) \exp \big[ 2.461 (1) \big] \qquad \text{passenger is female} \\
\frac{\hat{p}_i}{1 - \hat{p}_i} = \exp \left( \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 X_{i, \texttt{age}} \right) (11.717).
\end{gather*}
> *The interpretation for `sex` is: "a woman was 11.713 times more likely to survive than not to when compared to a man while keeping everything else constant."*

