<!-- # BEGIN SOLUTION -->

> *The likelihood is mathematically equivalent to the joint PMF. Nevertheless, the likelihood is in function of the parameters $p_1, \dots, p_n$ given the observed training values $y_1, \dots , y_{n}$:*

$$
l(p_1, \dots, p_n \mid y_1, \dots , y_{n}) = \prod_{i = 1}^n p_i^{y_i} (1 - p_i)^{1 - y_i}.
$$

