## (Challenging) Q5.6. Manipulating the Link Function

rubric={reasoning:1}

We can show via Equation (\ref{eq:log_odds}) the following:

\begin{equation}
\label{eq:odds}
\frac{p_i}{1 - p_i} = \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}.
\end{equation}

Thus, using Equation (\ref{eq:odds}), show that:

\begin{equation}
\label{eq:complement}
1 - p_i = \frac{1}{1 + \exp \left( \beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j} \right)}.
\end{equation}

<!--
# BEGIN QUESTION
name: Q5-6-reasoning
manual: true
-->

**ANSWER:**

<!-- # BEGIN SOLUTION -->

\begin{gather*}
\frac{p_i}{1 - p_i} = \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} \\
p_i = (1 - p_i) \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} \\
p_i = \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} - p_i \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} \\
p_i + p_i \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} =  \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} \\
p_i \left[ 1 + \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} \right] = \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} \\
p_i = \frac{\exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}}{1 + \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}} \\
1 - p_i = 1 - \frac{\exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}}{1 + \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}} \\
1 - p_i = \frac{1 + \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)} - \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}}{1 + \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}} \\
1 - p_i = \frac{1}{1 + \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j X_{i, j}\right)}}.
\end{gather*}

