> *Now, we obtain the log-likelihood function along with the corresponding logarithmic properties:*

\begin{align*}
\log \left[ l(\beta_0, \dots, \beta_k \mid y_1, \dots , y_{n}, x_{1,1}, \dots, x_{1,k}, \dots, x_{n,1}, \dots, x_{n,k}) \right] &= \log \left\{ \prod_{i = 1}^n \frac{\left[ \exp{\left(\beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j x_{i, j}\right)} \right]^{y_i}}{1 + \exp \left( \beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j x_{i, j} \right)} \right\} \\
&= \sum_{i = 1}^n \Bigg\{ y_i \Bigg( \beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j x_{i, j} \Bigg) \\ 
& \qquad - \log \Bigg[ 1 +  \exp \Bigg( \beta_0 + \sum_{j = 1}^k \beta_j x_{i, j} \Bigg) \Bigg] \Bigg\}.
